{"title":"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The Grade 8 and Grade 9 students at Pascal S.S. were surveyed about puzzles. Their responses are summarized in the chart shown, but two of the entries in the chart were erased. In total, how many Grade 9 students were surveyed?\n</p><p>(table with 92 students in 8th grade that didn't like puzzles, 140 students that didn't like puzzles, 125 students that did like puzzles, and 68 students in 9th grade that did like puzzles)\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/2/3f217f6442235d9b9abbefa69816b67e42a5b6bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 140 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 125 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 116 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 160 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 149$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"479\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From the table, we can see that there were <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/5/0b51850ccd3440214d4ccfbc14d29b2a31bfda55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$140$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> students in total that didn't like puzzles and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/3/403d424cf0f48517174037a871a71d9c35f1796e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$92$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> of them were in 8th grade, and the rest of them were in 9th grade. Thus, there were <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/d/08d1ed2efa1c562a2618d9e40179da1862f311e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$140 - 92 = 48$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"112\" height=\"15\" /> 9th grade students that didn't like puzzles.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>After adding that value to the table, we can see that of the students surveyed, the number of 9th graders was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/4/2e46d82791251bd70e9dd459ff9d9305dcf94e40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$68 + 48 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(C) } 116}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"158\" height=\"30\" />. \n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can realize that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/1/9e16e3504da8dac8e417cd7c1f5e44291cf195c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$125 + 140 = 265$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"130\" height=\"15\" /> students in total. \n</p><p>From the table, we can realize that there were <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/2/b829a6f0810a25e9ca9f85d690f2bafd0f2c1773.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$125$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> students in total that liked puzzles and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/8/9782dd7447f84ce6adcf7945b86038e379c618f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$68$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> of them were in 9th grade, and the rest of them were in 8th grade. Thus, there were <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/8/408e4de659681154e3aae2e0d028f8a617723d3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$125 - 68 = 57$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"112\" height=\"15\" /> 8th grade students that didn't\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>After adding that value to the table, we can see that of the students surveyed, the number of 8th graders was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/9/c190dc1ecb1157917d02ba82b75b543d3b2bf200.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$57 + 92 = 149$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"112\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Since there were <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/4/b848614cce96e8899ec50264dff44d08c2a25253.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$265$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> students in total and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/c/9ac7aa4fe47f55808896713ce8fcd30b954e59a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$149$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> were 8th graders, the number of surveyed 9th graders was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/a/5baeaa1d510be43efa6ec9354a72bf0dd4af4301.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$265 - 149 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(C) } 116}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"176\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal (page does not exist)\">2025 CEMC Pascal</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_8\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Probl